@node Language changes
@unnumbered Language changes
@node Incompatibilities with R5RS
@section Incompatibilities with @value{R5RS}
This section enumerates the incompatibilities between this report and
the @quotedbl{@value{Revised5} report}@footnote{@value{refR5RS}}.

This list is not authoritative, but is believed to be correct and
complete.

@itemize @bullet
@item
Case sensitivity is now the default in symbols and character names.
This means that code written under the assumption that symbols could be
written @samp{FOO} or @samp{Foo} in some contexts and @samp{foo} in
other contexts can either be changed, be marked with the new
@nc{@hashchar{}!fold-case} directive, or be included in a library using
the @nc{include-ci} library declaration.  All standard identifiers are
entirely in lower case.

@item
The @nc{syntax-rules} construct now recognizes @samp{_} (underscore) as
a wildcard, which means it cannot be used as a syntax variable.  It can
still be used as a literal.

@item
The @value{R5RS} procedures @nc{exact->inexact} and @nc{inexact->exact}
have been renamed to their @value{R6RS} names, @code{inexact} and
@code{exact}, respectively, as these names are shorter and more correct.
The former names are still available in the @value{R5RS} library.

@item
The guarantee that string comparison (with @code{string<?} and the
related predicates) is a lexicographical extension of character
comparison (with @code{char<?} and the related predicates) has been
removed.

@item
Support for the @samp{@hashchar{}} character in numeric literals is no
longer required.

@item
Support for the letters @samp{s}, @samp{f}, @samp{d}, and @samp{l} as
exponent markers is no longer required.

@item
Implementations of @nc{string->number} are no longer permitted to return
@code{#f} when the argument contains an explicit radix prefix, and must
be compatible with @code{read} and the syntax of numbers in programs.

@item
The procedures @nc{transcript-on} and @nc{transcript-off} have been
removed.

@end itemize

@node Other language changes since R5RS
@section Other language changes since @value{R5RS}
This section enumerates the additional differences between this report
and the @quotedbl{@value{Revised5} report}@footnote{@value{refR5RS}}.

This list is not authoritative, but is believed to be correct and
complete.

@itemize @bullet
@item
Various minor ambiguities and unclarities in @value{R5RS} have been
cleaned up.

@item
Libraries have been added as a new program structure to improve
encapsulation and sharing of code.  Some existing and new identifiers
have been factored out into separate libraries.  Libraries can be
imported into other libraries or main programs, with controlled exposure
and renaming of identifiers.  The contents of a library can be made
conditional on the features of the implementation on which it is to be
used.  There is an @value{R5RS} compatibility library.

@item
The expressions types @code{include}, @nc{include-ci}, and
@nc{cond-expand} have been added to the base library; they have the same
semantics as the corresponding library declarations.

@item
Exceptions can now be signaled explicitly with @code{raise},
@nc{raise-continuable} or @code{error}, and can be handled with
@nc{with-exception-handler} and the @code{guard} syntax.  Any object can
specify an error condition; the implementation-defined conditions
signaled by @code{error} have a predicate to detect them and accessor
functions to retrieve the arguments passed to @code{error}.  Conditions
signaled by @code{read} and by file-related procedures also have
predicates to detect them.

@item
New disjoint types supporting access to multiple fields can be generated
with the @nc{define-record-type} of @acronym{SRFI
9}@footnote{@value{refSRFI9}}.

@item
Parameter objects can be created with @nc{make-parameter}, and
dynamically rebound with @code{parameterize}.  The procedures
@nc{current-input-port} and @nc{current-output-port} are now parameter
objects, as is the newly introduced @nc{current-error-port}.

@item
Support for promises has been enhanced based on @acronym{SRFI
45}@footnote{@value{refSRFI45}}.

@item
Bytevectors, vectors of exact integers in the range from 0 to 255
inclusive, have been added as a new disjoint type.  A subset of the
vector procedures is provided.  Bytevectors can be converted to and from
strings in accordance with the @acronym{UTF-8} character encoding.
Bytevectors have a datum representation and evaluate to themselves.

@item
Vector constants evaluate to themselves.

@item
The procedure @nc{read-line} is provided to make line-oriented textual
input simpler.

@item
The procedure @nc{flush-output-port} is provided to allow minimal
control of output port buffering.

@item
Ports can now be designated as textual or binary ports, with new
procedures for reading and writing binary data.  The new predicates
@nc{input-port-open?} and @nc{output-port-open?} return whether a port
is open or closed.  The new procedure @nc{close-port} now closes a port;
if the port has both input and output sides, both are closed.

@item
String ports have been added as a way to read and write characters to
and from strings, and bytevector ports to read and write bytes to and
from bytevectors.

@item
There are now @acronym{I/O} procedures specific to strings and
bytevectors.

@item
The @code{write} procedure now generates datum labels when applied to
circular objects.  The new procedure @nc{write-simple} never generates
labels; @nc{write-shared} generates labels for all shared and circular
structure.  The @code{display} procedure must not loop on circular
objects.

@item
The @value{R6RS} procedure @nc{eof-object} has been added.  Eof-objects
are now required to be a disjoint type.

@item
Syntax definitions are now allowed wherever variable definitions are.

@item
The @nc{syntax-rules} construct now allows the ellipsis symbol to be
specified explicitly instead of the default @samp{...}, allows template
escapes with an ellipsis-prefixed list, and allows tail patterns to
follow an ellipsis pattern.

@item
The @nc{syntax-error} syntax has been added as a way to signal immediate
and more informative errors when a macro is expanded.

@item
The @code{letrec*} binding construct has been added, and internal
@code{define} is specified in terms of it.

@item
Support for capturing multiple values has been enhanced with
@nc{define-values}, @nc{let-values}, and @nc{let*-values}.  Standard
expression types which contain a sequence of expressions now permit
passing zero or more than one value to the continuations of all
non-final expressions of the sequence.

@item
The @code{case} conditional now supports @code{=>} syntax analogous to
@code{cond} not only in regular clauses but in the @code{else} clause as
well.

@item
To support dispatching on the number of arguments passed to a procedure,
@nc{case-lambda} has been added in its own library.

@item
The convenience conditionals @code{when} and @code{unless} have been added.

@item
The behavior of @code{eqv?} on inexact numbers now conforms to the
@value{R6RS} definition.

@item
When applied to procedures, @code{eq?} and @code{eqv?} are permitted to
return different answers.

@item
The @value{R6RS} procedures @code{boolean=?} and @code{symbol=?} have
been added.

@item
Positive infinity, negative infinity, NaN, and negative inexact zero
have been added to the numeric tower as inexact values with the written
representations @ns{+inf.0}, @ns{-inf.0}, @ns{+nan.0}, and @ns{-0.0}
respectively.  Support for them is not required.  The representation
@ns{-nan.0} is synonymous with @ns{+nan.0}.

@item
The @code{log} procedure now accepts a second argument specifying the
logarithm base.

@item
The procedures @code{map} and @nc{for-each} are now required to terminate
on the shortest argument list.

@item
The procedures @code{member} and @code{assoc} now take an optional third
argument specifying the equality predicate to be used.

@item
The numeric procedures @code{finite?}, @code{infinite?}, @code{nan?},
@nc{exact-integer?}, @code{square}, and @nc{exact-integer-sqrt} have
been added.

@item
The @code{-} and @code{/} procedures and the character and string
comparison predicates are now required to support more than two
arguments.

@item
The forms @samp{#true} and @samp{#false} are now supported as well as
@samp{#t} and @samp{#f}.

@item
The procedures @nc{make-list}, @nc{list-copy}, @nc{list-set!},
@nc{string-map}, @nc{string-for-each}, @nc{string->vector},
@nc{vector-append}, @nc{vector-copy}, @nc{vector-map},
@nc{vector-for-each}, @nc{vector->string}, @nc{vector-copy!}, and
@nc{string-copy!} have been added to round out the sequence operations.

@item
Some string and vector procedures support processing of part of a string
or vector using optional @var{start} and @var{end} arguments.

@item
Some list procedures are now defined on circular lists.

@item
Implementations may provide any subset of the full Unicode repertoire
that includes @acronym{ASCII}, but implementations must support any such
subset in a way consistent with Unicode.  Various character and string
procedures have been extended accordingly, and case conversion
procedures added for strings.  String comparison is no longer required
to be consistent with character comparison, which is based solely on
Unicode scalar values.  The new @nc{digit-value} procedure has been
added to obtain the numerical value of a numeric character.

@item
There are now two additional comment syntaxes: @samp{@hashchar{};} to
skip the next datum, and @ns{@hashchar{}| @value{defdots} |@hashchar{}}
for nestable block comments.

@item
Data prefixed with datum labels @ns{@hashchar{}@sv{n}=} can be
referenced with @ns{@hashchar{}@sv{n}@hashchar{}}, allowing for reading
and writing of data with shared structure.

@item
Strings and symbols now allow mnemonic and numeric escape sequences, and
the list of named characters has been extended.

@item
The procedures @nc{file-exists?} and @nc{delete-file} are available in
the @nc{(scheme file)} library.

@item
An interface to the system environment, command line, and process exit
status is available in the @nc{(scheme process-context)} library.

@item
Procedures for accessing time-related values are available in the
@nc{(scheme time)} library.

@item
A less irregular set of integer division operators is provided with new
and clearer names.

@item
The @code{load} procedure now accepts a second argument specifying the
environment to load into.

@item
The @nc{call-with-current-continuation} procedure now has the synonym
@nc{call/cc}.

@item
The semantics of read-eval-print loops are now partly prescribed,
requiring the redefinition of procedures, but not syntax keywords, to
have retroactive effect.

@item
The formal semantics now handles @nc{dynamic-wind}.
@end itemize

@node Incompatibilities with R6RS
@section Incompatibilities with @value{R6RS}
This section enumerates the incompatibilities between @value{R7RS} and
the @quotedbl{@value{Revised6} report}@footnote{@value{refR6RS}} and its
accompanying Standard Libraries document.

This list is not authoritative, and is possibly incomplete.

@itemize @bullet

@item
@value{R7RS} libraries begin with the keyword @nc{define-library} rather
than @nc{library} in order to make them syntactically distinguishable
from @value{R6RS} libraries.  In @value{R7RS} terms, the body of an
@value{R6RS} library consists of a single export declaration followed by
a single import declaration, followed by commands and definitions.  In
@value{R7RS}, commands and definitions are not permitted directly within
the body: they have to be be wrapped in a @nc{begin} library
declaration.

@item
There is no direct @value{R6RS} equivalent of the @nc{include},
@nc{include-ci}, @nc{include-library-declarations}, or @nc{cond-expand}
library declarations.  On the other hand, the @value{R7RS} library
syntax does not support phase or version specifications.

@item
The grouping of standardized identifiers into libraries is different
from the @value{R6RS} approach.  In particular, procedures which are
optional in @value{R5RS}, either expressly or by implication, have been
removed from the base library.  Only the base library itself is an
absolute requirement.

@cindex identifier syntax
@item
No form of identifier syntax is provided.

@item
Internal syntax definitions are allowed, but uses of a syntax form
cannot appear before its definition; the @nobr{@t{even}/@t{odd}} example
given in @value{R6RS} is not allowed.

@item
The @value{R6RS} exception system was incorporated as-is, but the
condition types have been left unspecified.  In particular, where
@value{R6RS} requires a condition of a specified type to be signaled,
@value{R7RS} says only @quotedbl{it is an error}, leaving the question
of signaling open.

@item
Full Unicode support is not required.  Normalization is not provided.
Character comparisons are defined by Unicode, but string comparisons are
implementation-dependent.  Non-Unicode characters are permitted.

@item
The full numeric tower is optional as in @value{R5RS}, but optional
support for @acronym{IEEE} infinities, NaN, and @minus{}0.0 was adopted
from @value{R6RS}.  Most clarifications on numeric results were also
adopted, but the @value{R6RS} procedures @nc{real-valued?},
@nc{rational-valued?}, and @nc{integer-valued}? were not.  The
@value{R6RS} division operators @code{div}, @code{mod},
@nc{div-and-mod}, @code{div0}, @code{mod0} and @nc{div0-and-mod0} are
not provided.

@item
When a result is unspecified, it is still required to be a single value.
However, non-final expressions in a body can return any number of
values.

@item
The semantics of @code{map} and @nc{for-each} have been changed to use
the @acronym{SRFI 1}@footnote{@value{refSRFI1}} early termination
behavior.  Likewise, @code{assoc} and @code{member} take an optional
@code{equal?}  argument as in @acronym{SRFI 1}, instead of the separate
@code{assp} and @code{memp} procedures of @value{R6RS}.

@item
The @value{R6RS} @code{quasiquote} clarifications have been adopted,
with the exception of multiple-argument @code{unquote} and
@nc{unquote-splicing}.

@cindex mantissa widths
@item
The @value{R6RS} method of specifying mantissa widths was not adopted.

@item
String ports are compatible with @acronym{SRFI
6}@footnote{@value{refSRFI6}} rather than @value{R6RS}.

@item
@value{R6RS}-style bytevectors are included, but only the unsigned byte
(@samp{u8}) procedures have been provided.  The lexical syntax uses
@samp{#u8} for compatibility with @acronym{SRFI
4}@footnote{@value{refSRFI4}}, rather than the @value{R6RS}
@samp{@hashchar{}vu8} style.

@item
The utility macros @code{when} and @code{unless} are provided, but their
result is left unspecified.

@item
The remaining features of the Standard Libraries document were left to
future standardization efforts.
@end itemize
